  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the maintainer of the smiley search, I want captures of the search requests exactly as the app sends them, so that LOT-053's flow is checked against HFR's real answers and not only against the raw-`+` captures `R53a`-`R53c`.\n\n### Scope\n\nPlain GETs on `https://forum.hardware.fr/message-smi-mp-aj.php?config=hfr.inc&findsmilies=…`, logged in (user2, as `R53a`-`R53c`) unless said otherwise, each with its LOT-005 oracle (`smiley-search`):\n\n- `findsmilies=chat` (one word, no `+`): same answer as `R53b` (`+chat`)?\n- `findsmilies=chat%20noir` (what the app and legacy send): same answer as `R53c` (`+chat+noir`, 1010 smileys)?\n- `findsmilies=%2Bchat%20%2Bnoir` (\"all keywords\", legacy `AnswerView.swift:1308-1318` @ `2440d79`): does a literal `+` make HFR AND the words?\n- A search with accents or special characters (e.g. `éclair`), and one returning standard (non-personal) smileys (LOT-025 spec).\n- The same `findsmilies=chat` logged out.\n- The wiki page of a code unknown to the wiki: `wikismilies.php?config=hfr.inc&detail=%5B%3Azzqxwunknown%5D`.\n\nAnonymize per docs/FIXTURES.md (personal smiley names are pseudos).\n\n### Lots that want it\n\n- LOT-053 (#79): `docs/lots/LOT-053-smiley-search-wiki.md`, \"Requests sent and captured\" and *pending capture*.\n- LOT-025 (#53, done): the special-character and standard-smiley states it listed as pending.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The captures and their oracles in `Packages/HFRKit/Tests/HFRParsingTests/Fixtures/`, anonymized, with meta files.\n- [ ] HFR-PROTOCOL §6c `### LOT-053` updated with what each encoding returns.\n",
